---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Installation"
  description="Install NGMS with Docker Compose, configure environment variables, and complete first boot."
  section="how-to"
  prev={{ title: 'Quick Start',     href: '/how-to' }}
  next={{ title: 'Adding Indexers', href: '/how-to/indexers' }}
>

<h1>Installation</h1>
<p class="page-meta">Docker Compose is the recommended deployment method.</p>

<h2>Docker Compose setup</h2>

<p>
  Create a directory for NGMS, save the following as <code>docker-compose.yml</code>, and
  customize the volume paths.
</p>

<div class="code-block">
  <div class="code-block-header">
    <span class="code-dot code-dot-r"></span>
    <span class="code-dot code-dot-y"></span>
    <span class="code-dot code-dot-g"></span>
    <span class="code-block-title">docker-compose.yml</span>
  </div>
  <pre><span class="comment">---</span>
<span class="key">services</span><span class="comment">:</span>

  <span class="key">postgres</span><span class="comment">:</span>
    <span class="key">image</span><span class="comment">:</span> <span class="val">postgres:17-alpine</span>
    <span class="key">restart</span><span class="comment">:</span> <span class="val">unless-stopped</span>
    <span class="key">environment</span><span class="comment">:</span>
      <span class="key">POSTGRES_USER</span><span class="comment">:</span>     <span class="val">ngms</span>
      <span class="key">POSTGRES_PASSWORD</span><span class="comment">:</span> <span class="val">changeme</span>
      <span class="key">POSTGRES_DB</span><span class="comment">:</span>       <span class="val">ngms</span>
    <span class="key">volumes</span><span class="comment">:</span>
      <span class="comment">- ./data/postgres:/var/lib/postgresql/data</span>
    <span class="key">healthcheck</span><span class="comment">:</span>
      <span class="key">test</span><span class="comment">:</span> <span class="val">["CMD-SHELL", "pg_isready -U ngms"]</span>
      <span class="key">interval</span><span class="comment">:</span> <span class="val">5s</span>
      <span class="key">retries</span><span class="comment">:</span> <span class="val">5</span>

  <span class="key">ngms</span><span class="comment">:</span>
    <span class="key">image</span><span class="comment">:</span> <span class="val">ghcr.io/ausagentsmith-org/stackarr:latest</span>
    <span class="key">restart</span><span class="comment">:</span> <span class="val">unless-stopped</span>
    <span class="key">depends_on</span><span class="comment">:</span>
      <span class="key">postgres</span><span class="comment">:</span>
        <span class="key">condition</span><span class="comment">:</span> <span class="val">service_healthy</span>
    <span class="key">ports</span><span class="comment">:</span>
      <span class="comment">- "9111:9111"</span>
    <span class="key">environment</span><span class="comment">:</span>
      <span class="key">DATABASE_URL</span><span class="comment">:</span> <span class="val">postgres://ngms:changeme@postgres:5432/ngms</span>
      <span class="key">STACKARR_PORT</span><span class="comment">:</span> <span class="val">9111</span>
      <span class="comment"># Optional — set a fixed API key instead of generating one</span>
      <span class="comment"># STACKARR_API_KEY: your-api-key-here</span>
    <span class="key">volumes</span><span class="comment">:</span>
      <span class="comment">- ./config:/config             # app config and DB migrations</span>
      <span class="comment">- /path/to/tv:/media/tv        # root folder for series</span>
      <span class="comment">- /path/to/movies:/media/movies # root folder for movies</span>
      <span class="comment">- /path/to/downloads:/downloads # download client staging</span></pre>
</div>

<div class="callout callout-warning">
  <span class="callout-icon">⚠</span>
  <div class="callout-body">
    <strong>Change the Postgres password</strong> before deploying. The default
    <code>changeme</code> is for illustration only — use a strong unique password.
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Start the stack</h2>

<div class="code-block">
  <div class="code-block-header">
    <span class="code-dot code-dot-r"></span>
    <span class="code-dot code-dot-y"></span>
    <span class="code-dot code-dot-g"></span>
    <span class="code-block-title">shell</span>
  </div>
  <pre><span class="cmd">docker compose up -d</span>
<span class="comment"># Wait for both containers to be healthy</span>
<span class="cmd">docker compose ps</span></pre>
</div>

<p>
  NGMS is now reachable at <code>http://your-host:9111</code>. On first access it redirects to
  the First Boot Wizard.
</p>

<h2>First Boot Wizard</h2>

<p>The wizard walks you through six steps — you can complete them now or skip and configure later.</p>

<div class="step">
  <div class="step-num">1</div>
  <div class="step-body">
    <h3>Admin account</h3>
    <p>Create your admin username and password. This is the first user with the <code>Owner</code>
    role — all subsequent users are created from <strong>Settings → Users</strong>.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="step">
  <div class="step-num">2</div>
  <div class="step-body">
    <h3>Authentication method</h3>
    <p>Choose <strong>Forms auth</strong> (username + password) or <strong>External auth</strong>
    (reverse proxy provides a trusted <code>X-Remote-User</code> header). Most installs use Forms.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="step">
  <div class="step-num">3</div>
  <div class="step-body">
    <h3>Root folders</h3>
    <p>Add the paths where NGMS should put organized series and movies. These must match the
    container volume mounts — e.g. <code>/media/tv</code> and <code>/media/movies</code>.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="step">
  <div class="step-num">4</div>
  <div class="step-body">
    <h3>Download client</h3>
    <p>Choose embedded torrent, embedded usenet, or configure an external client. You can add
    more clients after setup from <strong>Settings → Download Clients</strong>.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="step">
  <div class="step-num">5</div>
  <div class="step-body">
    <h3>Indexers</h3>
    <p>Add at least one indexer so NGMS can search for releases. Newznab (usenet) and Torznab
    (torrent) require an API URL + key from your indexer provider. Cardigann definitions
    require no key.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="step">
  <div class="step-num">6</div>
  <div class="step-body">
    <h3>Done</h3>
    <p>NGMS is ready. The wizard redirects to the main UI. Add your first series or movie to
    verify the full pipeline works end-to-end.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Environment variables reference</h2>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Variable</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>DATABASE_URL</code></td><td><em>required</em></td><td>PostgreSQL connection string</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>STACKARR_PORT</code></td><td><code>9111</code></td><td>HTTP port NGMS listens on</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>STACKARR_API_KEY</code></td><td>auto-generated</td><td>Override the generated API key</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>STACKARR_LOG_LEVEL</code></td><td><code>info</code></td><td><code>error</code> / <code>warn</code> / <code>info</code> / <code>debug</code> / <code>trace</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>STACKARR_CONFIG_PATH</code></td><td><code>/config</code></td><td>Directory for config file and migrations</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>STACKARR_*</code></td><td>—</td><td>All TOML config keys are settable via env var with this prefix</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Updating</h2>

<div class="code-block">
  <div class="code-block-header">
    <span class="code-dot code-dot-r"></span>
    <span class="code-dot code-dot-y"></span>
    <span class="code-dot code-dot-g"></span>
    <span class="code-block-title">shell</span>
  </div>
  <pre><span class="cmd">docker compose pull</span>
<span class="cmd">docker compose up -d</span>
<span class="comment"># Database migrations run automatically on startup</span></pre>
</div>

<div class="callout callout-tip">
  <span class="callout-icon">✦</span>
  <div class="callout-body">
    <strong>Hard links for space efficiency.</strong> If your download staging directory and media
    root folders are on the same filesystem (same Docker volume mount or bind mount), NGMS uses
    hard links during import — effectively zero-copy. Files won't count double against disk space.
  </div>
</div>

</DocsLayout>
